# See https://help.github.com/articles/ignoring-files/ for more about ignoring files.

# dependencies
/node_modules
/.pnp
.pnp.*
.yarn/*
!.yarn/patches
!.yarn/plugins
!.yarn/releases
!.yarn/versions

# testing
/coverage

# next.js
/.next/
/out/

# production
/build

# misc
.DS_Store
*.pem

# debug
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.pnpm-debug.log*

# env files (can opt-in for committing if needed)
.env*

# vercel
.vercel

# typescript
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts

# local design/reference screenshots -- not site assets, not committed
/.reference/

# NOTE: the Forever-era tile pyramids (public/map/{eastern-kingdoms,
# kalimdor}/tiles/) used to be excluded here and were local-only -- reversed
# 2026-09-25 once actual size was confirmed modest (~69MB / 2,406 files for
# both continents combined) and committed directly instead, so the deployed
# site can serve the real map. See CLAUDE.md's world-map architecture notes
# and docs/map-tile-cdn-plan.md (the future Classic-era toggle, whose source
# images are far larger, is planned to use object storage + a CDN instead of
# git -- don't commit those the same way without reading that doc first).

# Client-extracted world-map pin icons (dungeon/raid/battleground entrance
# art, once extracted from the atlas texture -- see CLAUDE.md's "entrance
# icon art" session note) -- same local-only/gitignored policy as the tiles
# above, not a site asset until a rights decision is made before deploying.
public/map/icons/

# Raw per-chunk AreaId grid cache (scripts/build-zone-areas.js), 2MB/continent
# -- a build artifact for that script's own re-runs (so later work on zone
# labels doesn't need to re-parse every ADT), not source data. The small
# derived public/map/*/zone-areas.json this script also writes is NOT
# ignored -- that's the real deliverable.
data/sources/client-db2/*/zone-grid-*.bin

# One-off debug renders (scripts/build-zone-areas.js's check-e image, zone
# polygons drawn over the z3 tile mosaic) -- a local eyeball-check artifact,
# not a site asset or committed data. Regenerate by re-running that script.
/debug-output/
